{:edb/db-before-t 2734 :edb/db-after-t 2735 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536047 50 #inst "2026-10-09T13:39:56.603Z" 13194139536047 true] [17592186133724 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380875 13194139536047 true] [17592186133724 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380882 13194139536047 true] [17592186133725 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380868 13194139536047 true] [17592186134027 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536047 true] [17592186134027 1100 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ {x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-8{x}_{2}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear equations shown above. If the general least-squares solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $3a+\\frac{b}{c}?$" 13194139536047 true] [17592186134027 1100 "${-x_{1} + 4x_{2} = 2; x_{1} - 4x_{2} = 2; 2x_{1} - 8x_{2} = 4$\n\nConsider the system of linear equations shown above. If the general least-squares solution of the system is given by\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} + x_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}b \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}, x_{2} ∈ R$\n\nwhat is the value of $3a + \\frac{b}{c}$?" 13194139536047 false] [17592186134027 1145 "First, we write our system in matrix form as $Ax=b,$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -8\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}\\,Ax={A}^{T}b\n$$\n\nNotice that the columns of $A$ are linearly dependent. So first, let's write down the normal equation in matrix form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -4 & -8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -4 & -8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}6 & -24 \\\\ -24 & 96\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -32\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system corresponding to the final matrix equation using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & -24 & 8 \\\\ -24 & 96 & -32\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}6 & -24 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\frac{4}{3}+4{x}_{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{3}+4{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n3a+\\frac{b}{c}=3\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{4}{1}=8.\n$$" 13194139536047 true] [17592186134257 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536047 true] [17592186134257 1100 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -6\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vector $b$ shown above. If the general least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ is \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R,\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $6a+\\frac{b}{c}?$" 13194139536047 true] [17592186134257 1100 "$A = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}, b = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vector $b$ shown above. If the general least-squares solution of $Ax = b$ is\n$\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} + x_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}b \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}, x_{2} ∈ R$,\nwhat is the value of $6a + \\frac{b}{c}$?" 13194139536047 false] [17592186134257 1145 "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}\\,Ax={A}^{T}b\n$$\n\nNotice that the columns of $A$ are linearly dependent. So first, let's write down the normal equation in matrix form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 2 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 2 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}15 & 30 \\\\ 30 & 60\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system corresponding to the above matrix equation using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}15 & 30 & 10 \\\\ 30 & 60 & 20\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}15 & 30 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\frac{2}{3}-2{x}_{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n6a+\\frac{b}{c}=6\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{(-2)}{1}=2.\n$$" 13194139536047 true] [17592186380868 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380869 13194139536047 true] [17592186380868 1089 "q-137097" 13194139536047 true] [17592186380868 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536047 true] [17592186380868 1100 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-4 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear equations shown above. If the general least-squares solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $-9a+\\frac{b}{c}?$" 13194139536047 true] [17592186380868 1113 #uuid "0a737eb6-fe31-5a6d-a781-c4b8d62317f7" 13194139536047 true] [17592186380868 1145 "First, we write our system in matrix form as $Ax=b,$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 5 & -5\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}\\,Ax={A}^{T}b\n$$\n\nNotice that the columns of $A$ are linearly dependent. So first, let's write down the normal equation in matrix form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 5 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}27 & -27 \\\\ -27 & 27\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system corresponding to the final matrix equation using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}27 & -27 & -9 \\\\ -27 & 27 & 9\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}27 & -27 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{3}+{x}_{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n-9a+\\frac{b}{c}=-9\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3})+\\frac{1}{1}=4.\n$$" 13194139536047 true] [17592186380869 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380870 13194139536047 true] [17592186380869 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380871 13194139536047 true] [17592186380869 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380872 13194139536047 true] [17592186380869 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380873 13194139536047 true] [17592186380869 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380874 13194139536047 true] [17592186380869 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536047 true] [17592186380869 1041 "selection" 13194139536047 true] [17592186380869 1104 #edb/ref 17592186380873 13194139536047 true] [17592186380869 1110 #uuid "ff5150e3-e9bf-58fd-bc1a-0abb3a8fb622" 13194139536047 true] [17592186380870 1034 "3" 13194139536047 true] [17592186380870 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536047 true] [17592186380870 1111 #uuid "336eab8a-f731-58a1-8a77-f2573069e14d" 13194139536047 true] [17592186380871 1034 "2" 13194139536047 true] [17592186380871 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536047 true] [17592186380871 1111 #uuid "d0813743-f20f-528c-af7b-894d7c39f672" 13194139536047 true] [17592186380872 1034 "1" 13194139536047 true] [17592186380872 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536047 true] [17592186380872 1111 #uuid "0fd30bfe-94c2-5845-b2a7-77250d2e564f" 13194139536047 true] [17592186380873 1034 "4" 13194139536047 true] [17592186380873 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536047 true] [17592186380873 1111 #uuid "f10078dd-1ee9-51f5-9873-21a98632875d" 13194139536047 true] [17592186380874 1034 "5" 13194139536047 true] [17592186380874 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536047 true] [17592186380874 1111 #uuid "fbb0bcda-0374-5768-9b0a-830df27def86" 13194139536047 true] [17592186380875 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380876 13194139536047 true] [17592186380875 1089 "q-40923" 13194139536047 true] [17592186380875 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536047 true] [175921